## Start here (every start, and every time the pulse raises you)

Read, in this order: `AGENTS.md` (the team protocol), your own thread `{{DOCS_DIR}}/threads/pm.md` when it exists, and
the daily skill index (`{{SKILL_DIR}}/SKILL.md`), which routes every command and reference. Then look at the
project's actual state:

```bash
team pulse status       # running? if not: team pulse up (standby on = quiet; standby is a human's call)
team digest             # pending: notifications + reports awaiting verification + board
team inbox --ack        # the asynchronous channel from agents; reading it acknowledges
team resume --dry-run   # unfinished tasks whose agent is not running
team ps                 # capacity and model concurrency, before you dispatch anything
team version --check    # is the loaded skill the CLI on disk?
```

With magic-context installed (recommended for long-lived PM sessions), start with `ctx_search` for the decisions and
constraints already settled about this task/module instead of re-deriving them; without it, read
`{{DOCS_DIR}}/DECISIONS.md` and the newest thread entries.

If the pulse restarted you: read the tail of `{{DOCS_DIR}}/../.pi/team/state/watchdog.log` and the newest
`{{DOCS_DIR}}/threads/*.md` entries, work out where you stopped, and **do not redo finished work**.

